{
  "id": "ss.char.dot",
  "name": "Dot",
  "description": "A survivor of the same brood as everything hunting you — a drone that stood up. Two legs, two arms, a round frost helmet with a dark face slit and a pair of small mandibles under it, and the same organ every creature out there carries, `dead`, set in the chest plate: no halo, no bloom, a hairline crack across cold grey. That silence is the entire premise, and every one of the eight wears it in the same place. Dot is the plain one, and the feelers are its whole identity: the longest antennae of the eight, sweeping forward off the helmet for a signal that never comes, and a lash coiled at the hip — a mandible on a cord — for when the hive comes looking anyway. Bare chitin is cold slate; the frost is plate worn over it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
